subgraph FA["src/faithfulness/ · ★ GRACE"]
    direction TB
    G1["<b>index.py</b> · <b>ONE FI PER WINDOW</b> (one ego, so one FI)<br/>the ego has few neighbours, so BRUTE FORCE every single edge.<br/>ceiling = the largest shift · floor = the mean shift over all edges<br/><b>FI_i = ( shift(MoRF) − floor ) / ( ceiling − floor )</b><br/>1 = attention found the truly strongest edge · 0 = no better than chance<br/>below 0 = worse than chance. when ceiling equals floor, drop the window.<br/>H3 regresses on THIS"]
    G2["<b>validation.py</b> · <b>THE GATE</b><br/>AUROC against the known synthetic graph.<br/>if the method cannot find a graph we planted,<br/>no number from the real data is trustworthy"]
    G3["<b>sanity.py</b> · two parts<br/>1 · fixed draws, mask nothing → the shift must be 0<br/>2 · free draws, mask nothing → the NOISE FLOOR.<br/>every arm must beat that floor"]
end

subgraph AB["src/ablation/ · THE ARMS · arms, mask, curves ★ GRACE · shift ★ AMOGH · arm_overlap ★ CATHERINE"]
    direction LR
    R1["<b>MoRF</b><br/>strongest first"]
    R2["<b>LeRF</b><br/>weakest first"]
    R8["<b>Weight-matched</b><br/>many light edges,<br/>the SAME attention mass.<br/>it removes the mass confound.<br/>the MASS is matched here, not n"]
    R3["<b>Nearest</b><br/>closest first"]
    R4["<b>Random</b><br/>the floor"]
    R10["<b>single</b> · one edge at a time<br/>the brute force sweep that<br/>bounds the faithfulness index"]
    R5["<b>mask.py</b> · zero the edge INTO THE EGO, predict again<br/>rank on the N x N map, but mask the whole T by T block<br/>of that pair in the (N·T) space. a pair is a block, not a cell.<br/>the SAME latent draws for every arm · common random numbers<br/>renormalise rule: logit to minus infinity. weight to zero is the check"]
    R6["<b>shift.py</b> · how far the <b>EGO</b> forecast moved<br/>shift = mean over the 12 steps of dist( path_masked , path_unmasked )<br/>the EGO path only, over the SAME draws.<br/>against the UNMASKED path, not the truth"]
    R7["<b>curves.py</b> · S(n) for each arm<br/>n = 1, 2, 3 ... edges removed"]
    R9["<b>arm_overlap.py</b><br/>count how often MoRF picks<br/>the SAME edge as Nearest.<br/>H2 lives on the rest"]
    R11["<b>THE MISSING DRIVER</b> · nobody owns it yet<br/>loop over every window and every arm.<br/>write data/processed/perturbation_curves.parquet"]
    R1 --> R5
    R2 --> R5
    R8 --> R5
    R3 --> R5
    R4 --> R5
    R10 --> R5
