subgraph HY["src/hypotheses/ · one file, one claim · design.py ★ PREM · the other 6 files ★ PREM, still to write"]
    direction TB
    Y0["<b>design.py</b> · BUILT AND FROZEN · one-sided · alpha = 0.05<br/>stride 5 · 571 windows · design effect 3.18 · effective n 179<br/>minimum effect 0.592 · power 0.80 · PRIMARY n_removed = 1.<br/>the sweep is secondary. the rest is exploratory.<br/>the design effect comes from eda/overlap.py. the hash is committed.<br/>the PRIMARY family is exactly 3 tests: H1, H2, H3. Holm covers those 3.<br/>MoRF against Random, MoRF against Weight-matched and the<br/>rank correlations SUPPORT the claim. They do not enter the family"]
    subgraph CH["<b>choose_test.py</b> · TO WRITE · the test must fit the distribution"]
        direction LR
        K1["<b>1 · the design is paired</b><br/>same window, two arms<br/>→ use the differences D_i"]
        K2["<b>2 · find the shape of D</b><br/>histogram · QQ plot · skew<br/>Shapiro-Wilk on D<br/>report the shape, do not assume it"]
        K3["<b>3a · symmetric</b><br/>→ Wilcoxon signed-rank, one-sided.<br/>it tests the PSEUDOMEDIAN.<br/>that equals the median only<br/>when D is symmetric. say so"]
        K4["<b>3b · skewed or heavy tail</b><br/>→ sign test on the median,<br/>or bootstrap the median of D.<br/>never a plain t-test"]
        K5["<b>4 · the rows are NOT independent</b><br/>windows overlap · pedestrians repeat · only 5 scenes<br/>→ p from permutation INSIDE the scene<br/>→ CI from the cluster bootstrap"]
        K1 --> K2
        K2 --> K3
        K2 --> K4
        K6["<b>5 · why NOT the other tests</b><br/>paired t-test → D is long-tailed. the mean is not the target<br/>plain bootstrap → it assumes independent rows. they are not<br/>OLS or ANOVA on raw rows → the same independence fault<br/>Bonferroni → Holm dominates it at no cost<br/>chi-square → the outcome is continuous, not a count"]
        K3 --> K5
        K4 --> K5
        K5 --> K6
    end
    YC["<b>data_checks.py</b> · TO WRITE · check that the input fits the test<br/>every window has every arm · no missing pair · print the attrition table<br/>zero differences: keep them, use the Pratt rule · the small window is dropped"]
    Y1["<b>h1_morf_vs_lerf.py</b> · TO WRITE<br/>D_i = shift(MoRF) − shift(LeRF)<br/>H0-1: median(D) is zero or less<br/>also report MoRF against Random<br/>and MoRF against Weight-matched"]
    Y2["<b>h2_beyond_proximity.py</b> · TO WRITE<br/>D_i = shift(MoRF) − shift(Nearest)<br/>H0-2: removal of high-attention edges does<br/>NOT give a larger forecast shift than<br/>removal of the nearest-neighbour edges.<br/>the ARM comparison is the primary test.<br/>Spearman rho( rank_attn , rank_dist ) and the partial<br/>correlation of attn with shift GIVEN distance SUPPORT it"]
    Y3["<b>h3_context.py</b> · TO WRITE<br/>FI_i = b0 + b·context + <b>scene FIXED effects</b><br/>context = density, n_agents,<br/>closing_speed, inv_ttc<br/>H0-3: every b = 0 AND every scene term = 0.<br/>ONE joint test. 5 scenes is too few for a<br/>random intercept. check the collinearity first.<br/>cluster-robust errors by pedestrian. report partial R2"]
    YV["<b>validate.py</b> · TO WRITE · check that the answer holds<br/>LOSO · n_removed sweep · another module · another time collapse · both mask rules.<br/>LOSO shows heterogeneity. it is NOT 5 more tests.<br/>If MoRF does not beat Random above the noise floor, the answer is<br/>'attention is NOT faithful'. That is a result, not a failure."]
    Y0 --> CH
    CH --> YC
    YC --> Y1 & Y2 & Y3
    Y1 & Y2 & Y3 --> YV
end
subgraph ST["src/stats/ · effects.py ★ CATHERINE · loso.py ★ GRACE · the other 4 files ★ PREM, still to write"]
    direction TB
    T1["<b>clustered.py</b> · TO WRITE · the primary unit is the <b>CONNECTED COMPONENT</b><br/>of the pedestrian by time-block graph. config.CLUSTER_UNIT holds it.<br/>the pedestrian and the time block CROSS: 37 percent of pedestrians<br/>span more than 1 block, so neither unit nests inside the other.<br/>a pilot of 2,418 real windows gives the false positive rate against<br/>a target of 0.05: pedestrian 0.085 · time block 0.115 · component 0.030.<br/>the component is the coarsest unit that respects both. 39 clusters.<br/>H1 and H2 → resample COMPONENTS with replacement, the pairs bootstrap.<br/>H3 → wild cluster bootstrap on the regression residuals.<br/>they are not the same tool. print n_clusters beside every p"]
    T6["<b>permutation.py</b> · TO WRITE · where the p-value comes from<br/>PRIMARY: flip the SIGN of D_i inside the cluster.<br/>exact for a paired design and it needs no GPU.<br/>SECONDARY: shuffle the attention weights inside the<br/>scene and re-rank. it holds the graph shape but it<br/>needs a new forward pass, so it is expensive"]
    T2["<b>loso.py</b><br/>per-scene estimate ·<br/>heterogeneity · jackknife"]
    T3["<b>effects.py</b><br/>rank-biserial r · Cliff delta<br/>Spearman rho · partial correlation.<br/>an effect, not just a p"]
    T4["<b>correction.py</b> · TO WRITE<br/>Holm over the 3 PRIMARY tests.<br/>Benjamini-Hochberg over the exploratory family"]
    T5["<b>report.py</b> · TO WRITE · one row per claim:<br/>test used · why · effect · CI · p_adj · n_clusters · verdict"]
    T1 --> T4
    T6 --> T4
    T2 --> T4
    T3 --> T4
    T4 --> T5
end

